+# Blog links in the user profile (MDL-88683)
+
+## Summary
+
+With the Classic theme being removed, the Navigation block is no longer the way to reach
+the site-wide blog. The user profile now offers a direct path to both personal and
+site-wide blog entries in the Boost theme.
+
+## What has changed
+
+In the **Miscellaneous** section of the user profile, when blogs are enabled:
+
+| Link | Destination | Notes |
+|------|-------------|-------|
+| **View my blog entries** | Your own blog entries (`/blog/index.php?userid=...`) | Previously labelled "Blog entries". When the profile is viewed from within a course, the course is kept as a filter, as before. |
+| **View site blog entries** | The site blog (`/blog/index.php`) | New link. |
+
+When you view another user's profile, the personal link keeps its existing label,
+"View all blog entries", and the new "View site blog entries" link is shown beside it.
+
+Both links appear only in the situations where the profile blog link appeared before:
+
+- blogs are enabled on the site (*Site administration > Advanced features > Enable blogs*),
+- the profile does not belong to the guest user, and
+- the person viewing is allowed to view that user's blog entries.
+
+When blogs are disabled, neither link is shown.
+
+## What has not changed
+
+- Blog permissions, capabilities and the **Blog visibility** setting work as before.
+  For example, when blog visibility is set to "Users can only see their own blog",
+  following "View site blog entries" shows the user's own entries only.
+- The blog pages themselves look and behave as before.
+
+## Steps to reach the site blog in Boost
+
+1. Open the user menu and select **Profile**.
+2. In the **Miscellaneous** section, select **View site blog entries**.
